<%# What the search box in the sidebar answers with.

    One block per conversation, best hit first. The ranking is the store's —
    bm25 over three weighted columns — so the conversation where the phrase was
    actually discussed arrives before the twenty where it appeared inside a tool
    result, and grouping keeps that order instead of imposing another.

    A hit is a link to the message itself, not to the conversation: the reader
    typed a phrase to find the place it was said, and handing them the tail of a
    long session would leave them scrolling for it. The snippet is the store's
    own, already escaped and already marked — see Store#snippet_html. -%>
<% if query.empty? -%>
<p class="search-hint"><%= h(I18n.t("web.search.hint")) %></p>
<% elsif groups.empty? -%>
<p class="search-hint"><%= h(I18n.t("web.search.no_match", query: query)) %></p>
<% else -%>
<nav class="search-results" aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.search.results")) %>">
  <% groups.each do |session_id, hits| -%>
  <% first = hits.first -%>
  <div class="search-group">
    <a class="search-head" href="/s/<%= h(session_id) %><%= h(token_query) %>"
       title="<%= h(first[:persona_label]) %> · <%= h(first[:title]) %>">
      <span class="emoji" aria-hidden="true"><%= h(first[:emoji]) %></span>
      <span class="label"><%= h(first[:title]) %></span>
      <span class="meta"><%= h(first[:age]) %></span>
    </a>
    <ul class="search-hits">
      <% hits.each do |hit| -%>
      <li>
        <a class="search-hit" href="<%= h(hit[:href]) %>">
          <span class="who"><%= h(hit[:who]) %></span>
          <span class="snippet"><%= hit[:html] %></span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <% end -%>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <% end -%>
</nav>
<% end -%>
